{
  "narrative": "Met with Marcus from TorqVance Machining (about 300 staff, export ~85% of their automated heat-treat rigs to EU markets). We went through their spec sheet for the new thermal press series to solve drift issues in curing; this is a brand new design line with no incumbent sensor vendor in place. He mentioned their visitor badges were updated to RFID last week. The engineering team is in technical review right now and plans to place volume orders within eight months for their Q4 build. Marcus emphasized their baseline spec: the sensor head has to run continuously at 300 degrees Celsius. The customer states that this requirement cannot be changed. He had no objections during our discussion.",
  "pain_points": [
    "drift issues in curing"
  ],
  "objections": []
}

{
  "narrative": "Met with Greg, lead eng at a mid-sized fluid systems OEM that exports over 80% of its automated skids to Latin America and the EU. We are deep in the technical review for their new polymer dosing skid. They built this platform from scratch, so they don't have an incumbent flow sensor vendor lined up for it. Greg mentioned their chief chemist is retiring next month. Their current setup relies on slow manual batch checks which cause severe filling bottlenecks. He handed over the engineering spec sheet: the process fluid measured by the flow sensor has a viscosity of 4500 millipascal-seconds. The customer states that this requirement cannot be changed. PO release is slated for October to hit their Q4 delivery milestone.",
  "pain_points": [
    "slow manual batch checks",
    "severe filling bottlenecks"
  ],
  "objections": []
}

{
  "narrative": "Met with Dan, VP of Procurement at Apex Domestic Milling (over 3,500 staff across 12 domestic grain facilities, zero export sales). Their chief engineer signed off yesterday, confirming our ceramic pressure sensor specs fully meet their boiler retrofit requirements. Dan needs to issue the PO immediately this week so maintenance can install them during the scheduled plant shutdown on Monday. However, Dan is pushing back hard during commercial terms negotiation. He stated our unit price is roughly 14% higher than what they currently pay their incumbent sensor vendor, Vance Instruments. He noted Vance has supplied their plants for eight years, but repeated sensor drift during summer milling cycles caused severe batch downtime. Dan also mentioned their main office cafeteria switched to a new coffee vendor this morning. He wants a price reduction matching Vance before signing off on the agreement.",
  "pain_points": [
    "repeated sensor drift",
    "severe batch downtime"
  ],
  "objections": [
    "unit price is roughly 14% higher"
  ]
}

{
  "narrative": "Caught up with Sarah (Procurement) and Dave (Lead Eng) at Apex Conveyor Systems, ~220 staff here in Ohio. Most of their packaging cells are exported to Germany and Mexico. Dave showed me their test bench and confirmed our displacement sensor specs match their new roller tolerances 100%. He noted their incumbent brand has frequent field failures on export units, which is costing them overseas warranty claims. They need to issue a PO this Friday to keep the export run on schedule. Sarah looked over our proposal and immediately flagged the cost, saying our unit price is 18% higher than what they currently pay the incumbent and well above their targeted bill-of-materials budget. On a side note, their plant parking lot is getting repaved so parking was a mess.",
  "pain_points": [
    "frequent field failures on export units",
    "overseas warranty claims"
  ],
  "objections": [
    "unit price is 18% higher",
    "well above their targeted bill-of-materials budget"
  ]
}

{
  "narrative": "Had an initial chat with Mark, founder of a 20-person shop making customized vacuum drying ovens. 80% of their machines export to semiconductor packaging plants in Taiwan and Germany. They currently source digital pressure sensors from SensorTech. Mark verified their final spec document is locked—needs 0 to 100 kPa absolute with Modbus RTU, signed off by their engineering lead. He noted they plan to place the order within six months for their Q3 manufacturing run. He expressed doubts about switching, stating our sensors are unproven in high-vibration vacuum pumps and could fail prematurely in foreign plants where maintenance is difficult. Mentioned their company parking lot is being repaved this week.",
  "pain_points": [],
  "objections": [
    "unproven in high-vibration vacuum pumps",
    "could fail prematurely in foreign plants"
  ]
}
